Z||000007||wkayl||06-07-2001||11:29 PM||||That link above will tell you where to get one and what the wiring is.  The sensor on my pickup is just right of center ahead of A/C condenser and grill.  There is a perfect hole in the support in front of the Fiero radiator to mount it. I didn't use the truck wiring because it was too hard to remove.  I just went to the hardware store and got some telephone wire.  I picked up some black wire covering (that ribbed stuff to hide the wires) so you couldn't see the wires under my 'hood'.  If I have time I may be able to take some pictures tomorrow. <BR>Boy I like spell check!!<P>------------------<BR>   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/sig_2.jpg"> <BR>Dnyee's 88 Formula, Casey's 86GT, Wayne's 86GT.  <BR>We consider my wife as being "Fiero Challenged"||||reg||1
